    "pooled_test_raw_edge": 0.0989,
    "frac_of_edge_explained_by_BLIND_BAND": 0.789,
    "why": "most of the held specialists' raw weather edge (78.9pct of it) is just the BLIND mid-favorite BAND mispricing {'c_71_82': 0.186, 'd_82_90': 0.081, 'e_90_98': 0.032}; their pooled skill-OVER-BLIND on the disjoint TEST week is only +2.09pp \u2014 and that residual is SELECTED-ON-TRAIN (survivorship) out of 1507 screened, so it is nowhere near Bonferroni-significant. Widening the voter set adds signal VOLUME, not per-dollar LB.",
    "converges_with_WS4": "WS4 found the \u22653-backer CONSENSUS adds no skill over a single sharp. WS2 finds the TRADERS add ~no skill over the blind band. Same conclusion from two directions: the weather edge is a PRICE-BAND property, NOT a trader/consensus property. Follow the BAND, not the people.",
    "action": "do NOT build a specialist voter arm. If weather is pursued, the honest form is a BLIND mid-favorite weather rule (0.71-0.90) \u2014 which still must clear the forward executable-ask gate (WS1: +1.87c haircut vs sharp fill; thin books, liq arm fires 0)."
  },
